--TEST--
A `///` run with nothing under it documents nothing and is refused, `#[` opens an attribute rather than a comment so an undeclared name inside it is reported, and a block comment that is never closed runs to the end of the file and is refused (`rule:tooling/doc-comment-attaches-to-the-next-declaration`, `rule:tooling/doc-comment-is-three-slashes`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: lang:programs/comments
// `rule:tooling/doc-comment-attaches-to-the-next-declaration`: a doc comment
// belongs to the declaration below it across no blank line. A blank line
// leaves it documenting nothing, and a note to the reader is `//`.
/// Documents nothing at all.

echo "never", "\n";

// `rule:tooling/doc-comment-is-three-slashes`: `#` opens a comment but `#[`
// opens an attribute, so what follows is read as a name rather than skipped.
#[Unwritten]
class Sample {
    public static function run(): int { return 1; }
}

/* A block comment ends at its first closing marker, and this one never writes
   one, so it runs to the end of the file and takes the statement below with it.
echo "also never", "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0127]: this doc comment is attached to nothing
%A
error[E0303]: `Unwritten` is not declared
%A
error[E0002]: unterminated block comment
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
